  "title": "[FeCl4]2- tetrahedral, quintet, ROHF/def2-SVP",
  "description": "Fe(II) is d6, so in a tetrahedral field the high-spin quintet is the ground state and the singlet lies well above it. This is the entry that shows the workflow is not Ni-specific, and it spans a larger spin range than the d8 pairs.",
